  "name": "Question 5",
  "problem": "Written in **ascending order**, the solutions to $|6-k|=2$ are $k=${{field-1}} and $k=$\n{{field-2}}.",
  "worked_solution": "Either the positive or negative of the expression inside the absolute value must be equal to the right-hand side of the equation.\n\nSo, we set up the two corresponding equations and solve them independently:\n\n- If $|6-k|=6-k,$ we obtain:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}|6-k| & =2 \\\\ 6-k & =2 \\\\ -k & =-4 \\\\ k & =4\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n- If $|6-k|=-(6-k),$ we obtain:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}|6-k| & =2 \\\\ -(6-k) & =2 \\\\ -6+k & =2 \\\\ k & =8\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, in ascending order, the solutions are $k=4$ and $k=8.$",
